# Trivy ignore list — each entry MUST carry a justification + exposure note.
# Reviewed 2026-10-31 (updated 2026-11-19). Only
# genuinely-unfixable-or-not-exploitable items belong here; everything else
# must be fixed, not suppressed.

# --- Litestream bundled-binary findings (v0.5.18, latest release) ----------
# Both CVEs live in the Go code INSIDE the third-party Litestream binary, not
# in our application. Litestream v0.5.18 (2026-11-03) is the newest release and
# ships with go-jose v4.1.4 + Go stdlib 1.26.10 — neither has an upstream
# release carrying the fix yet. Building Litestream from source with a patched
# Go toolchain is the only "fix" and is disproportionate for this app.
# EXPOSURE: Litestream runs as a replication CLIENT inside the container; its
# HTTP/1 server surface (CVE-2026-97054) is not exposed — App Runner only
# publishes the app's port 8000. go-jose (CVE-2026-116587, DoS via crafted RSA
# JWKs) parses only Litestream's own configuration/registry material, never
# attacker-controlled input in our deployment.
# REVISIT: on the next Litestream release — remove these entries, bump the
# Dockerfile pin, re-verify. (Local check: scripts/trivy_local.sh)
CVE-2026-97054
CVE-2026-116587

# --- Carried over from the v0.5.17 era: still present in the v0.5.18 binary ---
# x/net v0.60.0 remains in the v0.5.18 build (fix is v0.62.0). Exposure
# unchanged: Litestream parses no HTML — it is an S3 replication client only.
CVE-2026-78661   # x/net/html — DoS via crafted HTML (Litestream parses no HTML; S3 client only)

# --- Starlette CVEs whose ONLY fix is Starlette 1.x ---
# FastAPI (even latest 0.120.x) pins `starlette<0.50.0`, so we cannot adopt the
# 1.x fix lines without FastAPI itself moving to Starlette 1.x (future upstream).
# We DID fix the one 0.49.x-addressable CVE (CVE-2025-62727) by pinning
# starlette==0.49.2. The two below are accepted with the exposure noted:
#
# CVE-2026-48818 — StaticFiles SSRF / UNC-path credential theft.
#   Exposure: our only StaticFiles mount serves the built SPA /assets dir
#   (server-controlled, no user-supplied paths); the SPA catch-all has a
#   path-containment guard (main.py). Not reachable with attacker-controlled input.
CVE-2026-48818
#
# CVE-2026-54283 — request.form() size limits silently ignored (form DoS).
#   Exposure: the app enforces its own request-body-size cap in the security
#   middleware (1MB JSON / 50MB upload via Content-Length), which bounds this.
CVE-2026-54283

# NOTE: Litestream was upgraded v0.3.13 -> v0.5.17 (2026-10-31), cutting the
# binary's findings from ~60 (incl. 3 CRITICAL) to 11 HIGH; the v0.5.17-era
# suppressions were retired when the binary moved to v0.5.18 (2026-11-19),
# which cleared all 11 and left only the two entries at the top of this file.
